% references.bib — M2 Biosciences bibliographic review (enslyonreview)
% Style: biblatex + biber, numeric-comp (Current Opinion-style numbered
% citations, compressed ranges, e.g. [8-10])
%
% Recommended: export your library from Zotero rather than typing entries by
% hand — see enslyonreview.pdf, section "Exporting your Zotero bibliography
% to LaTeX", for the Better BibTeX plug-in setup. Standard fields: author,
% title, journaltitle, year, volume, pages, doi. The custom fields pmid and
% pmcid (declared in enslyonreview.dbx) are NOT exported by Zotero — add
% them by hand if you want them to appear, bracketed, after the DOI.
%
% Keys follow the convention Better BibTeX generates: AuthorTitleYear
% (e.g. smithSomeExampleTitle2024).
%
% Add your first entry below, e.g.:
%
% @article{smithSomeExampleTitle2024,
%   author       = {Smith, John},
%   title        = {Some example title},
%   journaltitle = {Journal Name},
%   year         = {2024},
%   volume       = {12},
%   pages        = {1--10},
%   doi          = {10.xxxx/xxxxx},
% }
